33,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The minutes show the same flats kept the covered spots for five years without any review.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I saw the shoving match clearly. The rain makes the wet bikes harder to move, causing the delays.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"The ledger is empty for repairs. The ward park costs 2,600 yen, and fourteen people are already waiting there.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,The treasurer’s file shows three hours a month just for cash. Adding per-place billing would double that load.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The sticker register shows three bikes per flat, but the complaint log proves no one is actually managing the spots.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, if the rules are too strict, we risk turning neighbors into rivals. I want to avoid that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I understand, Misaki. But the physical struggle is real. We need a system that reduces the morning friction.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"If we charge 2,600 yen, we cover the ward park cost and the building gets a surplus. It’s simple math.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,But who does the billing? The last two jobs we invented landed on one person and then quietly lapsed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,The complaints died because there was no owner. We need a system that doesn’t rely on one person’s goodwill.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"A lottery might feel random, but it prevents the quiet resentment of permanent favorites.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,A lottery could work if it’s simple. I just want the morning to be peaceful and orderly for everyone.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"A lottery is free, but it doesn’t solve the money problem. The building needs income to fix the broken lights.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,A lottery requires someone to draw the names and post the results. That is still a recurring task.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we use a lottery, we can rotate the duty. No one person gets stuck with the administrative burden forever.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I think a simple lottery with rotating duties balances fairness and social peace.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It removes the daily struggle and the hidden resentment. It feels kind to everyone.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I still prefer the paid option. It brings in money and filters out those who don’t really need a spot.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"The paid option is too heavy for the treasurer. The lottery is lighter, but we must ensure the rotation works.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,Let’s go with the lottery. It breaks the cycle of favoritism and shares the small burden fairly among us.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
