60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option C, the annual lottery, seems best for keeping our relationships calm and avoiding daily conflict.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Misaki. The lottery removes the morning shoving match and the rain-related stress.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that actually pays for the building’s needs. The others are just free rides.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,Option A is too much work for the treasurer. Option C is manageable if we rotate the drawing duty.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option C is fair. It ensures everyone has an equal chance and stops the same doors from always winning.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I understand the need for funds, but Option A might create more friction than it solves.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,The physical comfort of the residents is more important to me than the surplus. Option C brings peace.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"If we don’t charge, the building account stays empty. We can’t fix the lights or the racks without money.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,The treasurer’s file is clear. Adding billing to the existing three hours a month is a recipe for burnout.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"The complaint log shows that unpaid, unmanaged spaces just rot. A lottery with rotating duties is the only sustainable path.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I am concerned that Option B, open racks, might lead to hoarding or blocking, which causes new conflicts.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Option B is too chaotic. I want a clear, predictable system. The lottery gives us that stability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,Option B is a disaster. People will just take up more space than they need. It’s a free-for-all.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,Option B requires constant monitoring to prevent hoarding. That is a full-time job for someone.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Option B is too vague. We need clear rules. The lottery provides a clear, fair, and manageable set of rules.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will vote for Option C. It balances fairness, social harmony, and manageable administrative effort.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will also vote for Option C. It brings peace to the mornings and respects everyone’s comfort.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"I will vote for Option A. We need the money to maintain the building, and this is the only way to get it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,I will vote for Option C. It is the least burdensome for the association and avoids the pitfalls of the other options.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I will vote for Option C. It breaks the cycle of favoritism and ensures equal opportunity for all residents.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
